      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I clicked by accident on unfavorite and don't know which group the users is put in before.... oh geez.\nI really need visible group name in the user window.......! Easy and useful for me. No big deal with small text. \n\nAnd \"favorite\" is still wrong name. \"group\" is more logic name. I understand it will put a yellow star on the picture, but it's just placed in the group. That is not-so-much-special compared to \"favorite\". I have 3 group named as Best friend, my country, other country. It's like add some information to user, so i can recognize user easier. Not to \"favorite\" him...\n\nYou have also groups in Whatsapp, not called as favorites... as example.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
