  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-09T14:46:44.633Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It's nice to have groups so i can put my friends in right groups to recognize them easier.\n\nBut there is still plenty room in user info tab, there should also group name placed when it's added to named group. You have already Favorite button there but it's not clear where the user is placed in the Favorite group. It just there 9/96 and that is all. Of course you can go back to Social but if you have so many friends... it takes more time to check it out.\n\nThat is why adding group name in user info tab will make more clear and better recognizeable. Especially if you click on Social tab and click for information about user (above row), you will see immediately if you have added it as friend and also in which group. If you forgot it, just click on Favorite button and put it in right group.\nAlso less mistakes if you want unfavorite the friend (euh... ungroup is better name - we need another button name, see below).\n\nThat should more helpful right with visible groupname, isn't it?\n\n* Note: Why is button named 'Favorite'? Is 'Group 9/96' not more logic name? You don't actually need to favorite it again, it's already your friend. It's just putting in the group, and that is different compared to 'Favorite'. 'Favorite group' sounds bit strange for me. 'Friend group' sounds more better. *",
